cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LRSinglecell, please cite the version of the pipeline you used
  (the Zenodo concept DOI below resolves to the latest release; each release
  has its own version DOI), together with nf-core/scnanoseq and the tools
  listed in CITATIONS.md.
title: "IntGenomicsLab/lrsinglecell"
abstract: >-
  LRSinglecell is a Nextflow pipeline for single-cell/nuclei long-read
  sequencing data from Oxford Nanopore. It processes 10X Genomics cDNA
  libraries (gene and isoform quantification) and single-cell DNA libraries,
  separately or together in one run (e.g. 10X Multiome), from raw FASTQ to
  cell-barcode-tagged, deduplicated BAMs, feature-barcode matrices and QC
  reports. It is derived from nf-core/scnanoseq.
type: software
# Authors follow the nextflow.config manifest and the README credits. Austyn
# Trull and Lara Ianov wrote nf-core/scnanoseq, from which this pipeline is
# derived.
authors:
  - family-names: Harbers
    given-names: Luuk
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3910-6497"
    affiliation: "VIB Center for Cancer Biology, VIB, Leuven, Belgium"
  - family-names: Trull
    given-names: Austyn
    affiliation: "University of Alabama at Birmingham, Birmingham, AL, USA"
  - family-names: Ianov
    given-names: Lara
    affiliation: "University of Alabama at Birmingham, Birmingham, AL, USA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IntGenomicsLab/lrsinglecell"
url: "https://github.com/IntGenomicsLab/lrsinglecell"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24341090"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24341090"
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions, resolves to the latest release"
  - type: doi
